&lt;p&gt;Across India, Singapore and Malaysia, our products span everything from seamless checkouts to payroll automation - powering a fintech ecosystem that’s redefining how money moves across Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, that ecosystem supports everyone from early-stage startups to some of India’s largest enterprises, enabling them to accept, process, and disburse payments at scale while expanding into new ways of managing money more efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our scale speaks volumes: Razorpay processes $180+ billion in annualized transactions, powering leading businesses like Airbnb, Facebook, WhatsApp, Airtel, CRED, BookmyShow, Zomato, Swiggy, Lenskart, Mirae Asset Capital markets, Indian Oil, National Pension Scheme - and over 100 of India’s unicorns. With strong roots in India and growing operations in Southeast Asia, we are shaping the next chapter of financial technology across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are backed by global investors including GIC, Peak XV Partners (formerly Sequoia Capital India &amp;amp; SEA), Tiger Global, Ribbit Capital, Matrix Partners, MasterCard, and Salesforce Ventures, having raised over $740 million to date. Strategic acquisitions - including Ezetap (POS and offline payments), Curlec (Malaysia expansion), BillMe (digital invoicing), and POP (rewards-first UPI) - along with earlier moves in fraud prevention, payroll, and lending, have further strengthened our platform and widened our footprint across Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But what truly sets Razorpay apart is our culture. At Razorpay, ownership is our oxygen - you own what you build, with no micromanagement or red tape, just the runway to make your ideas fly. Learning is a lifestyle - if you’re curious, you’ll feel at home here. People &amp;gt; Pedigree - we hire for attitude, hustle, and hunger more than degrees. Transparency thrives over titles - this is where interns question CXOs and CXOs say “thank you.” Guided by our values of Customer First, Autonomy &amp;amp; Ownership, Agility with Integrity, Transparency, Challenging the status quo and a strong belief that Razorpay grows with Razors,&amp;nbsp; you’ll be part of a 3000+ strong team building not just products, but the financial infrastructure of the future.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Manager, Cross Border (KAM) exists to govern, sustain, and exponentially grow relationships with Razorpay’s highest-revenue international and export-facing enterprise clients. This role solves the critical business problem of maximizing merchant lifetime value, navigating complex international payment requirements, and driving global portfolio retention.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Portfolio Strategy &amp;amp; Revenue:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the overarching growth and retention strategy for Razorpay&#39;s top-tier cross-border accounts, consistently exceeding portfolio quotas through aggressive cross-selling and up-selling of international and domestic payment solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Stakeholder Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Orchestrate CXO-level business reviews and build deep, long-lasting strategic partnerships with key decision-makers at global enterprise clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Orchestration:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate extensively with Product, Engineering, Compliance, and Legal teams to champion customized financial solutions that meet complex international regulatory (e.g., FEMA) and operational requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Escalation &amp;amp; SLA Governance:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the ultimate escalation authority for critical global client concerns, driving rapid resolution and ensuring strict adherence to international Service Level Agreements (SLAs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven Account Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Leverage cross-border market intelligence, FX routing trends, and CRM data repositories to proactively identify risks, optimize the account management lifecycle, and refine overarching international go-to-market strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications : &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional executive presence with advanced interpersonal, stakeholder influence, and global commercial negotiation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep strategic and analytical mindset with a strong understanding of international B2B payment ecosystems, cross-border regulations (e.g., FEMA, RBI export guidelines), multi-currency processing, and global enterprise operational models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead, mentor, and inspire a senior, quota-carrying key account management team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-6 years of relevant experience in Key Account Management, Enterprise Sales, or Strategic Partnerships within the B2B, SaaS, Fintech, or Cross-Border Payments space.&lt;/li&gt;
